# Normalise everything to LF in the repository.
#
# Development happens on Windows but the build runs on Vercel's Linux
# containers, and without this every file would land in the repo with CRLF.
# That is not cosmetic: it makes a one-character edit show as a whole-file
# diff, and it breaks shell scripts the moment one is added.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, convert it to LF on commit, and
# hand it back in the platform's own flavour on checkout. Nothing about the
# Windows working copy changes.
* text=auto

# Lockfiles are tooling-owned and enormous; never let a diff tool try to be
# clever about them in a review.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated=true
